{"step_index":1588,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:57:51Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:57:51+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-12T01:57:51+02:00\n\nThe command exited with code 0.\nOutput:\n{\"step_index\":1575,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T23:57:36Z\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"python3 -c \\\\\\\"\\\\nimport itertools\\\\nfrom collections import deque\\\\n\\\\ndef bfs_dists(adj, n, v):\\\\n    dist = {v: 0}\\\\n    q = deque([v])\\\\n    while q:\\\\n        curr = q.popleft()\\\\n        for nxt in adj[curr]:\\\\n            if nxt not in dist:\\\\n                dist[nxt] = dist[curr] + 1\\\\n                q.append(nxt)\\\\n    return dist\\\\n\\\\nn = 6\\\\nadj = {i: [] for i in range(n)}\\\\nfor i in range(n - 1):\\\\n    adj[i].append(i + 1)\\\\n    adj[i + 1].append(i)\\\\nf = (0, 2, 0, 0, 2, 0)\\\\nW = sum(f)\\\\nfor w in range(n):\\\\n    d = bfs_dists(adj, n, w)\\\\n    for k in range(n):\\\\n        compl = sum(1 for u in range(n) if d[u] > k)\\\\n        if k + compl + 1 <= W:\\\\n            print(f'w={w}, k={k}: compl={compl}, k+compl+1={k+compl+1} <= W={W}')\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"5000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Print witnesses for P_6\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Print witnesses for P_6\\\"\"}}]}\r\n{\"step_index\":1576,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"GENERIC\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T23:57:39Z\",\"content\":\"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:57:39+02:00\\nCompleted At: 2026-09-12T01:57:39+02:00\\n\\nThe command exited with code 0.\\nOutput:\\nw=2, k=2: compl=1, k+compl+1=4 <= W=4\\r\\nw=2, k=3: compl=0, k+compl+1=4 <= W=4\\r\\nw=3, k=2: compl=1, k+compl+1=4 <= W=4\\r\\nw=3, k=3: compl=0, k+compl+1=4 <= W=4\\r\\n\\n\"}\r\n{\"step_index\":1577,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T23:57:39Z\",\"thinking\":\"**Evaluating a specific graph case**\\n\\nConsidering the case where the width and a specific parameter are both 2, the inequality holds. Investigating a particular vertex (vertex 2) within a graph, it's connected to other vertices that appear to match the graph's structure. However, the graph's radius is 3. The branch condition relies on graph radius, which is relevant to this case.\\n\\n\\n**Analyzing the condition for contradiction**\\n\\nExamining previous successful cases, the condition `radius G + 1 <= romanWeight f` seems sufficient for automated solving. Conversely, the negation, `romanWeight f <= radius G` could lead to a contradiction. Considering the meaning of graph radius and Roman domination number, if the Roman domination number is less than or equal to the graph radius, a contradiction seems inevitable. This would mean that eccentricity of every vertex in the graph is greater or equal than the Roman domination number.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"python3 -c \\\\\\\"\\\\nimport itertools\\\\nfrom collections import deque\\\\n\\\\ndef bfs_ecc(adj, n, v):\\\\n    dist = {v: 0}\\\\n    q = deque([v])\\\\n    while q:\\\\n        curr = q.popleft()\\\\n        for nxt in adj[curr]:\\\\n            if nxt not in dist:\\\\n                dist[nxt] = dist[curr] + 1\\\\n                q.append(nxt)\\\\n    if len(dist) < n:\\\\n        return None\\\\n    return max(dist.values())\\\\n\\\\n# Can radius(G) >= romanWeight(f)?\\\\n# Let's test random trees of size up to 20\\\\nimport random\\\\nfound = False\\\\nfor trial in range(1000):\\\\n    n = random.randint(4, 18)\\\\n    prufer = [random.randint(0, n - 1) for _ in range(n - 2)]\\\\n    deg = [1] * n\\\\n    for x in prufer: deg[x] += 1\\\\n    adj = {i: [] for i in range(n)}\\\\n    for x in prufer:\\\\n        for y in range(n):\\\\n            if deg[y] == 1:\\\\n                adj[x].append(y); adj[y].append(x)\\\\n                deg[x] -= 1; deg[y] -= 1; break\\\\n    u, v = [i for i in range(n) if deg[i] == 1]\\\\n    adj[u].append(v); adj[v].append(u)\\\\n    rad = min(bfs_ecc(adj, n, i) for i in range(n))\\\\n    # We want to know if there is ANY Roman dominating function f with weight W <= rad!\\\\n    # If there is, that means rad >= W!\\\\n    # Does any f have W <= rad?\\\\n    # Test greedy / random or optimal f:\\\\n    # If the MINIMUM Roman domination number rdn <= rad, then YES!\\\\n    # Otherwise NO!\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"5000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Test if radius >= W is ever possible\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Test radius >= W\\\"\"}}]}\r\n{\"step_index\":1578,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"GENERIC\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T23:57:45Z\",\"content\":\"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:57:45+02:00\\nCompleted At: 2026-09-12T01:57:46+02:00\\n\\nThe command exited with code 0.\\nStdout:\\n\\nStderr:\\n\\n\"}\r\n{\"step_index\":1579,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T23:57:46Z\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"python3 -c \\\\\\\"\\\\nimport itertools\\\\nfrom collections import deque\\\\n\\\\ndef bfs_ecc(adj, n, v):\\\\n    dist = {v: 0}\\\\n    q = deque([v])\\\\n    while q:\\\\n        curr = q.popleft()\\\\n        for nxt in adj[curr]:\\\\n            if nxt not in dist:\\\\n                dist[nxt] = dist[curr] + 1\\\\n                q.append(nxt)\\\\n    if len(dist) < n:\\\\n        return None\\\\n    return max(dist.values())\\\\n\\\\ndef roman_domination_number(adj, n):\\\\n    min_w = 2 * n\\\\n    for f in itertools.product([0, 1, 2], repeat=n):\\\\n        w = sum(f)\\\\n        if w >= min_w: continue\\\\n        valid = True\\\\n        for v in range(n):\\\\n            if f[v] == 0 and not any(f[u] == 2 for u in adj[v]):\\\\n                valid = False; break\\\\n        if valid: min_w = w\\\\n    return min_w\\\\n\\\\n# Test all trees up to n=10\\\\nimport random\\\\nmax_ratio = 0\\\\nfor n in range(2, 11):\\\\n    for trial in range(50):\\\\n        if n == 2:\\\\n            adj = {0: [1], 1: [0]}\\\\n        else:\\\\n            prufer = [random.randint(0, n - 1) for _ in range(n - 2)]\\\\n            deg = [1] * n\\\\n            for x in prufer: deg[x] += 1\\\\n            adj = {i: [] for i in range(n)}\\\\n            for x in prufer:\\\\n                for y in range(n):\\\\n                    if deg[y] == 1:\\\\n                        adj[x].append(y); adj[y].append(x)\\\\n                        deg[x] -= 1; deg[y] -= 1; break\\\\n            u, v = [i for i in range(n) if deg[i] == 1]\\\\n            adj[u].append(v); adj[v].append(u)\\\\n        rad = min(bfs_ecc(adj, n, i) for i in range(n))\\\\n        rdn = roman_domination_number(adj, n)\\\\n        if rad >= rdn:\\\\n            print(f'rad >= rdn! n={n}, rad={rad}, rdn={rdn}')\\\\n        ratio = (rad + 1) / rdn\\\\n        if ratio > max_ratio:\\\\n            max_ratio = ratio\\\\nprint(f'Max (rad + 1) / rdn observed: {max_ratio}')\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"10000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Find max ratio of (rad + 1) / rdn\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Find max ratio\\\"\"}}]}\r\n{\"step_index\":1580,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"GENERIC\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T23:57:49Z\",\"content\":\"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:57:49+02:00\\nCompleted At: 2026-09-12T01:57:50+02:00\\n\\nThe command exited with code 0.\\nOutput:\\nMax (rad + 1) / rdn observed: 1.0\\r\\n\\n\"}\r\n\n"}
